        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Stephanocereus, Nepenthes\n- Places: Brazil, South China, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Madagascar, the Seychelles, Australia, New Caledonia, India, Sri Lanka\n- Concepts: cactus genus, liana-forming plants, Old World tropics\n\nFacts:\n- Stephanocereus is a genus of cactus from Brazil.\n- Stephanocereus is related to Arrojadoa.\n- Nepenthes are mostly liana-forming plants of the Old World tropics.\n- Nepenthes range from South China, Indonesia, Malaysia, and the Philippines westward to Madagascar and the Seychelles.\n- Nepenthes range southward to Australia and New Caledonia.\n- Nepenthes range northward to India and Sri Lanka.",
